000900*REMARKS.
001000*D   THIS SUBPROGRAM IS USED TO PREVENT BLOWUPS ON THE OPEN TERM
001100*D   CALL.  OFTEN, WE GET AN ERROR ON THE OPENTERM DUE TO BAD
001200*D   LINES.  HOWEVER A TERM RESET AND RETRY USUALLY WORKS.
001300*D   THIS SUBPROGRAM WILL TRY 7 TIMES TO OPEN THE TERMINAL.  IF
001400*D   ALL 7 FAIL, IT WILL RETURN WITH A BAD STATUS CODE.
      *  NOTE: FOR IBM THIS IS A DUMMY SUBPROGRAM AND DOES NOTHING.
